@* About — PinballWizard engineering story page.
 *
 * Public, anonymous-accessible page that tells the architecture story to
 * engineering-curious prospects. Linked from BrandFooter ("What we cover →")
 * and the /status footer link family.
 *
 * Content:
 *   - What PinballWizard is (1–2 sentences, from docs/vision.md)
 *   - Architecture summary: Blazor Web App + .NET Aspire + Azure + Clean Architecture + OTel
 *   - Architecture diagram (pre-rendered SVG; source of truth is
 *     docs/diagrams/about-architecture.mmd — regeneration instructions live
 *     in that file's header, and PreRenderedDiagramTests pins SVG <-> source
 *     agreement via an embedded SHA-256)
 *   - Tech stack bullets
 *   - How this was built (Claude Code as first-class engineering participant)
 *   - GitHub repo link
 *
 * The diagram is static-served, so the page needs no render mode, no
 * third-party script, and no CSP allowance — see the 2026-06-11
 * decision-log entry "Pre-rendered SVG replaces client-side Mermaid".
 *
 * Community-resource posture (ADR-0027 § 1): the page explains the app
 * honestly and routes users outward — no engagement-metric framing, no
 * "trending" copy, no signup gate.
 *
 * ADR-0008 — MudBlazor strict (MudText, MudLink, MudCard, MudList etc.)
 * ADR-0026 § chrome — not a delight surface; standard chrome component.
 *@

@page "/about"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using PinballWizard.Web.Components.Shared

<PageTitle>PinballWizard — About</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Large" Class="about-page" data-testid="about-page">

    @* ── Page header ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <AppPageHeader Title="About PinballWizard"
                   Subtitle="PinballWizard is an AI-powered pinball encyclopedia and repair assistant that answers questions grounded in first-party manufacturer data — manuals, service bulletins, and machine specifications — and routes every unanswerable question to the authoritative community resource that can help." />

    @* ── Architecture summary ─────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="about-section-heading mb-2 mt-4">
        Architecture
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-3">
        Built on Clean Architecture with .NET 10 and .NET Aspire, the system separates
        domain logic (Core), orchestration (Application), and infrastructure concerns
        (scrapers, community rulesheets, Cosmos DB, Azure AI Search) across four layers.
        Polite scrapers and community rulesheet synthesizers harvest first-party and
        community strategy documents into the RAG corpus; a Change-Feed-driven RAG
        Ingestion Worker chunks and embeds the manufacturer data into an Azure AI Search
        vector index. Azure AI Foundry orchestrates multi-agent reasoning (Wizard, Repair,
        Grounding, and Search agents) over those tools — every answer carries a clickable
        citation that deep-links to the source document or community guide.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
        OpenTelemetry wires structured traces, metrics, and logs end-to-end from the browser
        to the Azure Monitor workspace. An admin panel at <code>/admin</code> surfaces
        run-history, corpus statistics, ingestion monitoring, and per-manufacturer source detail
        — the same observability posture a production engagement would demand.
    </MudText>

    @* ── Architecture diagram ─────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <div class="about-diagram-container mb-6" data-testid="about-diagram">
        <MudImage Src="img/about-architecture.svg"
                  Alt="Architecture diagram showing four layers: Public Interface (Blazor Web App and Admin Panel) connects over HTTPS and SSE to the API and Application Layer (ASP.NET Core streaming endpoint and Azure AI Foundry with Microsoft Agent Framework). The AI Foundry calls tools against the Data Layer (Cosmos DB Serverless, AI Search Basic, Azure OpenAI). The offline Data Ingestion layer (10 polite scrapers, OPDB sync, community rulesheets, and RAG Ingestion Worker) feeds Cosmos and AI Search."
                  Fluid="true"
                  data-testid="about-diagram-svg"
                  Class="about-diagram-image" />
    </div>

    @* ── Tech stack ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="about-section-heading mb-2 mt-4">
        Tech Stack
    </MudText>

    <AppBulletList Class="about-tech-list mb-6" data-testid="about-tech-list">
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">.NET 10 / C# 14 — Clean Architecture (Core · Application · Infrastructure · Presentation)</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Blazor Web App + MudBlazor — public pages, document corpus browser, admin panel</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">.NET Aspire 13 — local orchestration with Cosmos + Azurite emulators</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Azure AI Foundry + Microsoft Agent Framework — multi-agent orchestration (Wizard · Repair · Grounding · Search)</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Azure OpenAI — gpt-4o reasoning + text-embedding-3-small for RAG</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Azure Cosmos DB Serverless — machines · documents · catalog stats (Change-Feed-driven)</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Azure AI Search Basic — vector + BM25 retrieval over the indexed document corpus</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Azure Container Apps — Web, API, and RAG Ingestion Worker</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">OpenTelemetry — structured traces, metrics, and logs to Azure Monitor</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Server-Sent Events (text/event-stream) — streaming answer delivery with citation deep-links</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
    </AppBulletList>

    @* ── How this was built ───────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="about-section-heading mb-2 mt-4" data-testid="about-claude-heading">
        How This Was Built
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
        PinballWizard is built with Claude Code as a first-class engineering participant — not
        autocomplete, but a peer held to the same discipline: feature branch, local review,
        mechanical PR audit, conventional commits. Most ADRs were decided <em>with</em> Claude,
        not just implemented by it.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
        The Claude Code configuration is owned in-repo, documented, and CI-guarded — skills,
        rules, commands, and agents live under <code>.claude/</code>, each carrying a provenance
        header, validated on every PR.
    </MudText>

    <AppBulletList Class="about-claude-list mb-6" data-testid="about-claude-list">
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudLink Href="https://github.com/Early-Bird-Solutions-LLC/PinballWizard/blob/main/docs/claude-code.md"
                     Target="_blank"
                     rel="noopener noreferrer"
                     aria-label="How this repo uses Claude Code (opens on GitHub)">
                How this repo uses Claude Code
            </MudLink>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudLink Href="https://github.com/Early-Bird-Solutions-LLC/PinballWizard/blob/main/docs/adr/0040-fork-claude-config-for-pinballwizard.md"
                     Target="_blank"
                     rel="noopener noreferrer"
                     aria-label="ADR-0040: forking the Claude Code config in-repo (opens on GitHub)">
                ADR-0040 — forking the config in-repo
            </MudLink>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudLink Href="https://github.com/Early-Bird-Solutions-LLC/PinballWizard/tree/main/.claude"
                     Target="_blank"
                     rel="noopener noreferrer"
                     aria-label=".claude/ configuration directory (opens on GitHub)">
                .claude/ configuration
            </MudLink>
        </AppBulletItem>
    </AppBulletList>

    @* ── What we cover ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="about-section-heading mb-2 mt-4">
        What We Cover
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
        PinballWizard has first-party data (manuals, service bulletins, game pages, machine specs)
        on 8 active manufacturers and OPDB. The full document corpus is browseable at
        <MudLink Href="/documents" aria-label="Browse the document corpus">
            /documents
        </MudLink>
        — filter by manufacturer, game, or document type, and follow each citation back to
        its source file:
    </MudText>

    <AppBulletList Class="about-manufacturer-list mb-2" data-testid="about-manufacturer-list">
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Stern Pinball — manuals, game pages, and service bulletins</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Jersey Jack Pinball</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">American Pinball</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Spooky Pinball</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Pinball Brothers</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Barrels of Fun</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Multimorphic</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Chicago Gaming Company</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">OPDB — Open Pinball Database (canonical machine catalog)</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
        <AppBulletItem>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Tilt Forums — community Wiki Rulesheets (~80-90 modern machines)</MudText>
        </AppBulletItem>
    </AppBulletList>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mb-4">
        Everything else routes to authoritative community resources — Pinside, IFPA, Pinball Map,
        and manufacturer sites — rather than attempting to answer from incomplete data.
    </MudText>

    @* ── Data partners ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <MudText id="data-partners" Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="about-section-heading mb-2 mt-2">
        Data Partners
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
        PinballWizard is built on direct partnerships with community operators. Every integration
        started with a direct ask to the person who built the resource — and every answer credits
        its source:
    </MudText>

    @* Four partner cards — same component as Landing, roomier (Compact=false). *@
    <div class="about-partners-grid mb-2" data-testid="about-data-partners-list">
        <DataPartnerCard Role="Catalog"
                         Name="OPDB"
                         Href="https://opdb.org"
                         Description="Open Pinball Database — the canonical machine catalog every integration pivots on."
                         StatusText="Canonical · active" />
        <DataPartnerCard Role="Rules"
                         Name="Kineticist"
                         Href="https://kineticist.com"
                         Description="Gameplay-rules depth and catalog enrichment via API access and rules-guide permission (Colin Alsheimer, Jun 2026)."
                         StatusText="API + rules · Jun 2026" />
        <DataPartnerCard Role="Rules"
                         Name="Tilt Forums"
                         Href="https://tiltforums.com"
                         Description="Community-maintained Wiki Rulesheets — deep strategy guides for modern machines (Greg Dunlap, Jul 2026)."
                         StatusText="Community · Jul 2026" />
        <DataPartnerCard Role="Pricing"
                         Name="Silverball Labs"
                         Href="https://silverballlabs.com"
                         Description="Live market pricing from Will Oetting (May 2026), drawn from the origin sales dataset at PinballPrices.com (Ted &#x22;Doc&#x22; Finlay)."
                         StatusText="Live pricing · May 2026" />
    </div>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mb-6">
        Attribution is required and present on every answer that draws from a partner's data.
    </MudText>

    @* ── GitHub link ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-3">
        The source code is open on
        <MudLink Href="https://github.com/Early-Bird-Solutions-LLC/PinballWizard"
                 Target="_blank"
                 rel="noopener noreferrer"
                 aria-label="PinballWizard on GitHub"
                 Class="about-github-link"
                 data-testid="about-github-link">
            GitHub
        </MudLink>.
        ADRs, build specs, and quality gates are committed alongside the code — the engineering
        story is readable in the repository, not just in this page.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-8">
        <MudLink Href="/engineering"
                 aria-label="Explore the engineering docs"
                 data-testid="about-engineering-link">
            Explore the engineering docs →
        </MudLink>
    </MudText>

</MudContainer>

<style>
    .about-diagram-container {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
        backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: 32px;
        box-shadow: 0 8px 32px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
        transition: all 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.165, 0.84, 0.44, 1);
        animation: diagramEntry 1s ease-out;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    .about-diagram-container:hover {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
        border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
        box-shadow: 0 12px 48px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
        transform: translateY(-4px);
    }

    .about-diagram-image {
        filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3));
        transition: transform 0.4s ease;
    }

    .about-diagram-container:hover .about-diagram-image {
        transform: scale(1.01);
    }

    @@keyframes diagramEntry {
        from { 
            opacity: 0; 
            transform: translateY(30px) scale(0.98); 
            filter: blur(10px);
        }
        to { 
            opacity: 1; 
            transform: translateY(0) scale(1); 
            filter: blur(0);
        }
    }

    .about-section-heading {
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        background: linear-gradient(90deg, #fff 0%, #aaa 100%);
        -webkit-background-clip: text;
        -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    }

    /* Adjust the partners grid for 4 items */
    .about-partners-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
        gap: 16px;
    }
</style>
